    "Sliver (degrees, 0 = off): needles (longest edge ≥ 4 × shortest, Botsch & Kobbelt 2001 / CGAL) are collapsed under the link condition, the end with the smaller quadric error goes (Garland & Heckbert 1997); caps (one angle near 180°) have their long edge flipped when that raises the smallest angle; border caps are dropped. No vertex is moved.",
